    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69087" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύκηρος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμυγδάλη</span>
			, <i>almond</i>, 
				Lacon.
			 and Tenian word, <i><span class="en">
				Seleuc.
			</span></i> ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				2.52c
			</span></i>: 
				Lacon.
			 also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μούκηρος</span></b> 
				Pamphil.ib.<i><span class="en">
				53b
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μουκηρόβατος</span></b>  (leg. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαγός</span>, i. e. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝᾱγός</span>
			from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγνυμι</span>), ὁ, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρυοκατάκτης</span>
			, Id.ibid.; written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μουκηρόβας</span></b>  in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
